    "narrative": "The Austin Waves' offense centers on **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) today, our clear top play. Despite facing a crafty arm in Sonny Gray, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a potent combination of a 16% park factor boost and a significant dynamic platoon advantage, cementing his status as a must-start at SS. Alongside him, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (68.14) provides high-floor production; while his platoon matchup against Seth Lugo is technically negative, his raw power profile and favorable SP_xERA environment keep his efficiency comfortably in the \"Strong\" range. **Heliot Ramos** (64.65) also earns a high-tier nod, as his ability to handle lefty pitching\u2014evidenced by a 19% boost from the matchup against Ray\u2014makes him an essential component of our outfield coverage.\n\nThe marginal decisions remain tight, particularly concerning **Kyle Tucker** (49.94). Although his base projections are usually elite, a low lineup slot against Cade Cavalli suppresses his efficiency, placing him just inside the active roster over **Liam Hicks** (39.70). **Liam Hicks** was the closest cut from our bench today; while his platoon advantage against Jacob deGrom is notable, the sheer elite nature of deGrom\u2019s skill profile ultimately capped his scoring potential, favoring the higher run-production environment surrounding **Kyle Tucker**. Elsewhere, **Sam Antonacci** (56.02) draws a recommendation thanks to his likely leadoff spot, which maximizes his limited-but-vital speed potential against Taj Bradley. \n\nWe must remain cautious of the \"Lineup Pending\" status for several key contributors like **Miguel Vargas** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**. If these players shift lower in the batting order or are pulled for rest, their efficiency scores will crater. Furthermore, while **Dominic Smith** (42.10) is currently active, his start is tenuous; he is only occupying a roster spot due to specific BvP history and the lack of a superior high-ceiling alternative for 